[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3657125581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114034#issuecomment-3657125581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114034","id":3657125581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Z-07N","user":{"login":"wenekar","id":100775364,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgG1xA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100775364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar","html_url":"https://github.com/wenekar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wenekar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-15T18:57:43Z","updated_at":"2025-12-15T18:57:43Z","body":"Narrowed issue down to window being maximized upon receiving .size = Vec2 assignment. Resizing while window is maximized does not work.\n\nIn the embedded window, setting .size to a new value resizes something, but engine resolution is still set to project resolution. I am unsure if this is intended or not.\n\n<img width=\"1620\" height=\"892\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/63b825cd-0387-4f96-9174-fc1e5bc1958d\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3657125581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3754258715","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114034#issuecomment-3754258715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114034","id":3754258715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fxXEb","user":{"login":"SteveSmith16384","id":8761942,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NjE5NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8761942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384","html_url":"https://github.com/SteveSmith16384","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T11:23:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T11:23:24Z","body":"This is also an issue in Godot 3.6.2.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3754258715/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5031841365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114034#issuecomment-5031841365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114034","id":5031841365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABK-vOVQ","user":{"login":"SteveSmith16384","id":8761942,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NjE5NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8761942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384","html_url":"https://github.com/SteveSmith16384","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SteveSmith16384/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T08:35:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T08:35:20Z","body":"I think I've found a workaround.  Set these two settings as follows, prior to setting the window size:\n\n\t\tOS.window_fullscreen = false\n\t\tOS.window_maximized = false\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5031841365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084385320","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114034#issuecomment-5084385320","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114034","id":5084385320,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLw2QKA","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-26T16:35:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-26T16:35:08Z","body":"Can you reproduce it on Windows or Wayland if you have access to it? I have tested on X11 XFCE, and it seems that `XResizeWindow` is ignored and lots of time is spent in timeout without any results. If smaller window size is set, everything goes through well once `XSync` is complete. Here's related code:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/159701651ad44335691dcbd632d8074307074c7b/platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp#L2727-L2738\n\n As far as I'm aware, window resizing is handled by window manager in X11, thus XFCE could have impacted my results. In my case, my monitor is 1920x1080, but it didn't need to be exactly monitor size for resizing to be ignored. 1920x1046 didn't want to resize, but 1290x1045 did want to resize.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5084385320/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5089301938","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114034#issuecomment-5089301938","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114034","id":5089301938,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABL1iVsg","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T08:57:05Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T08:57:05Z","body":"There are mainly 2 issues at hand. Firstly, window gets moved, resized and maximized differently than Godot requested when X11 window is mapped. It happens here.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/159701651ad44335691dcbd632d8074307074c7b/platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp#L1987-L1988\n\nThese lines show that window size is changed and maximized by window manager, and not by Godot. Window state can be inspected with `xwininfo -id 0x2000006 -all` (window ID varies). This was tested on 1920x1200 monitor.\n\n<img width=\"522\" height=\"281\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2413fef-3e25-4963-a874-bc6a52121ab4\" />\n\nNot much can be done there, only to respect what window manager provides. Setting maximization off before resizing is one example. Perhaps improving documentation to mention that setting size doesn't mean it will be set to that value exactly could help, or notifying that properties were not changed like they were expected to.\n\nThe workaround can be even shorter and it should support multiple windows too:\n```gdscript\nget_window().mode = Window.MODE_WINDOWED\nget_window().size = Vector2(400, 200)\n```\n\nSecond issue is that Godot in many parts of the code expects that whatever window properties it requested, those properties are applied exactly like that. In setting size scenario, that causes viewport size to get out of sync with window size, if window manager changes size unexpectedly or doesn't change size at all. Depending on where it is called, it causes flickering or stays out of sync, which is undesirable.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5089301938/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]